                "logprobs": [],
                "text": "On September 13, 2026, leaders from major AI labs—including Anthropic, SpaceXAI, OpenAI, and Google DeepMind—collectively called for a slowdown in AI development. Anthropic CEO Dario Amodei initiated this call, expressing concerns that rapid AI progress could lead to catastrophic scenarios within six months. His remarks were echoed by top executives such as Elon Musk, Sam Altman, and Demis Hassabis, who emphasized prioritizing safety over growth. This rare moment of unity within the competitive industry highlights a shared commitment to responsible AI development. ([axios.com](https://www.axios.com/newsletters/axios-am-68956162-ed74-42e1-a892-ae3da8e7d74f?utm_source=openai))\n\n\n## Highlights:\n- [\uD83D\uDEA6 Axios AM: Hitting AI brakes](https://www.axios.com/newsletters/axios-am-68956162-ed74-42e1-a892-ae3da8e7d74f?utm_source=openai), Published on Sunday, September 13\n- [Trump rejects pause in AI race citing competition from China](https://www.lemonde.fr/en/economy/article/2026/09/14/trump-rejects-pause-in-ai-race-citing-competition-from-china_6757508_19.html?utm_source=openai), Published on Monday, September 14 "
